<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM shares gain after Q1 results.</title>
<headline>KLM shares gain after Q1 results.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>KLM Royal Dutch Airlines' shares gained after the company reported higher than expected first quarter profits.</p>
<p>The shares were 2.40 guilders higher at 78.80 guilders in a modestly firmer Amsterdam stock market.</p>
<p>KLM reported net profit of 190 million guilders, down 81 million guilders from the first quarter of 1996 when the results included a sizeable contribution from partner Northwest Airlines . Analysts had forecast profit in the range 94-136 million guilders.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
